 R←Test_47(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ALIEN;list;fno;crash
⍝ A variable holding instances of a class cannot be written to a component file: `SaveCrash` must still
⍝ save the crash, without what cannot be serialised
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 #.⎕SHADOW'HandleErrorParms'
 #.HandleErrorParms←##.HandleError.CreateParms
 #.HandleErrorParms.killThreads←0                    ⍝ Killing threads would kill the session's own threads
 #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder←GetTempPath⊃⎕SI
 #.HandleErrorParms.saveErrorWS←0
 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP'
 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 {}#.TEMP.⎕FIX':Class Dummy' ':EndClass'
 ALIEN←(⎕NEW #.TEMP.Dummy)(⎕NEW #.TEMP.Dummy)        ⍝ Nameclass 2, so `SaveVisibleVars` collects it
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 {}'CREATE!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder

 ⎕TRAP←(405 'E' '406 ##.HandleError.Process #.HandleErrorParms')(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 :Trap 406
     {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}405
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :EndTrap

 →T.GoToTidyUp 406≠⎕EN
 list←FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.dcf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢list
 fno←(⊃list)⎕FTIE 0
 crash←⎕FREAD fno 1
 ⎕FUNTIE fno
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠⎕NC'crash'                          ⍝ Not just the message of the DOMAIN ERROR `⎕FAPPEND` ran into
 →T.GoToTidyUp 405≠crash.EN

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
